xamine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ corresponds to the system \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+9{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+20{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}-13{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 20 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -13 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -13 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+9{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ {x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ 5{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+2(\\mathbf{0})=\\mathbf{0}\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nand, substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(\\mathbf{0})+9(\\mathbf{0})=\\mathbf{0}\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=\\mathbf{0}.\n$$\n\nSince ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$, we get that the set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, statements I and III are false, while statement II is true." 13194139547118 17592186576411 false] [17592186564487 1074 "We say that three vectors ${\\mathbf{v}}_{1},{\\mathbf{v}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{v}}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Otherwise, the 